              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " number of contexts. Now, I noticed with my solution that many times, before the last context in the first test gets closed, the second test fails because it cant allocate the maximum number of contexts. On the other hand, when I add closing of the buffer descriptor inside the first test, everything works. So I'm wondering whether this is something I should somehow support? At the end of the day, file descriptors should be closed by the program that uses them, and while I don't leak resources when its not closed, because of that sometimes closing can happen too late."
